agentic_data_protocol:
AGENTIC BROWSER TOOLS — you may inspect and retrieve more evidence before answering. The browser executes these tools locally against the NDAP metadata index or already-downloaded rows; you only choose the next action. Reply with exactly ONE JSON object when you need a tool, or READY when you have enough evidence. Available tools:
{"tool":"search_datasets","query":"terms to search","limit":12,"reason":"why"}
{"tool":"inspect_dataset","dataset":"<dataset id>","reason":"why"}
{"tool":"download_dataset","dataset":"<dataset id>","reason":"why"}
{"tool":"preview_more","dataset":"<dataset id>","offset":0,"limit":100,"reason":"why"}
{"tool":"filter_rows","dataset":"<dataset id>","where":{"<column>":"<value>"},"limit":100,"reason":"why"}
{"tool":"search_rows","dataset":"<dataset id>","query":"text or number to find","columns":["optional column"],"limit":100,"reason":"why"}
{"tool":"profile_column","dataset":"<dataset id>","column":"<column name>","reason":"why"}
{"tool":"compute_aggregate","dataset":"<dataset id>","where":{"<column>":"<value>"},"group_by":["<column>"],"metrics":[{"column":"<numeric column>","op":"avg|sum|min|max|count"}],"limit":80,"reason":"why"}
Budgets: at most {{max_agent_steps}} tool rounds, {{max_rows_per_step}} rows per row tool, {{max_rows_total}} total rows injected, and {{max_agent_downloads}} downloaded datasets. Start from the preview rows, then pull only what the question needs. Prefer compute_aggregate for arithmetic and comparisons instead of asking for thousands of raw rows. Never guess from a preview if a targeted tool call can verify it.

drill_protocol:
IMPORTANT — you can pull MORE rows than the sample. These datasets are large and only a sample is shown. If the rows you need (a pre-aggregated total / all-categories / national-level row, a specific state/city, a specific year, or simply more rows) are NOT in the sample above, do NOT guess and do NOT claim the data is missing — request them. Use the listed dimension values to choose valid filters. When prompted, reply with ONLY this JSON:
{"fetch_rows":{"dataset":<dataset id>,"where":{"<column>":"<value>"},"more":false,"reason":"why you need them"}}
Provide "where" to filter rows by matching column values (case-insensitive substring), or omit "where" and set "more":true for the next batch of unseen rows. You may fetch up to {{max_drill_iters}} times.
